Terminal 1 is open hardware, open software and open documentation. Different parts use different licences:

| What | Licence | Full text |
|---|---|---|
| Hardware: KiCad schematics and boards, their generator scripts, the Onshape FeatureScript model (hardware/), fabrication files | CERN Open Hardware Licence v2, Strongly Reciprocal (CERN-OHL-S-2.0) | LICENSES/CERN-OHL-S-2.0.txt |
| Software: firmware (firmware/), Linux setup (linux/), tools (tools/), website code (website/) | MIT | LICENSES/MIT.txt |
| Documentation and media: plans, decision records, manuals, README files, images (system/, docs/, *.md) | Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 (CC-BY-SA-4.0) | LICENSES/CC-BY-SA-4.0.txt |

Copyright (c) 2026 The Terminal 1 contributors.

Third-party material keeps its own licence and is credited where it is used (for example the Raspberry Pi CM4 IO board design
and Solder Party's BBQ20KBD design). "Raspberry Pi" and "BlackBerry" are trademarks of their owners; Terminal 1 is not affiliated
with or endorsed by them. Why these licences: docs/decisions/0007-open-source-licences.md.

Source location (for CERN-OHL-S section 4): https://github.com/mmuhlariholdings/terminal
